---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import stage from '../../assets/portrait.webp';
import TestimonialSection from '../../components/TestimonialSection.astro';
---
<Base title="Speaking that starts a real conversation" description="Bring Loren Michaels Harris to your next event. Explore keynotes on leadership, resilience, and the stories that connect an audience.">
<section class="wrap service-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">KEYNOTES & SPEAKING</p><h1>Give your room<br/>a reason to<br/><span class="gold-text">lean in.</span></h1><p>For leadership teams, educators, and communities. Personal stories, honest questions, and a message shaped around the people in front of him.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/contact/?service=speaking">Discuss your event ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="#topics">Explore the topics ↓</a></div></div><figure><Image src={stage} alt="Loren speaking with an audience at an event" widths={[500,800,1200]} sizes="(max-width:767px) 100vw, 50vw" loading="eager"/><figcaption>In the room with Loren · Photograph: Scott R. Gane</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="section dark" id="topics"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">START WITH YOUR AUDIENCE</p><h2>What conversation<br/>does your room need?</h2><div class="topic-columns"><article><h3>Leadership & connection</h3><p>For teams exploring how they communicate, build trust, and show up for one another. Begin with the challenge your people are facing.</p></article><article><h3>Resilience & perspective</h3><p>For audiences navigating change or adversity. Loren draws on lived experience to open a conversation about how we understand our challenges.</p></article><article><h3>The power of your story</h3><p>For people finding their voice. Explore the connection between personal experience, an authentic message, and the people who hear it.</p></article></div><p class="form-note" style="margin-top:32px">The topic, session format, and intended takeaways are agreed around your event.</p></div></section>
<TestimonialSection compact/>
<section class="section wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">FOR EVENT ORGANIZERS</p><h2>From first inquiry<br/>to the right fit.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/media-kit/">Organizer resources ↗</a></div><div class="steps"><article class="step"><span class="number">01</span><h3>Tell us about the room.</h3><p>Share your date, location, audience, and the reason you’re bringing people together. An undecided date is welcome.</p></article><article class="step"><span class="number">02</span><h3>Shape the conversation.</h3><p>Discuss the event goals, a relevant topic, and the format that fits your schedule.</p></article><article class="step"><span class="number">03</span><h3>Confirm the details.</h3><p>Agree availability, scope, and practical arrangements before making a commitment.</p></article></div><div class="actions" style="margin-top:38px"><a class="button" href="/contact/?service=speaking">Discuss your event ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="section wrap"><p class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU ASK</p><h2>A few practical questions.</h2><div class="faq-group"><details><summary>Can the message reflect our audience?</summary><p>Share the people, goals, and context behind your event. Audience fit and the scope of customization are discussed before an engagement is agreed.</p></details><details><summary>What if our date or format isn’t final?</summary><p>You can inquire with an undecided date. Include your likely timing and whether you’re considering an in-person or virtual session.</p></details><details><summary>How do we discuss fees and availability?</summary><p>Use the <a href="/contact/?service=speaking">event inquiry</a> with your audience, location, and timing. Availability and fees are confirmed directly.</p></details></div></section>
</Base>
